/* About: This File

The first-run logging notice: what the local log contains, where it lives,
and an explicit on/off choice. Shown automatically on add-in load for as
long as the "LogLevel" user preference is unset - answering it (either
way) is what stops it appearing again, so there's no separate "already
shown" flag to keep in sync.

Cancelling does NOT count as consent: the preference stays unset,
nothing is logged, and the notice comes back next load.

Finer-grained levels (Warn, Debug) are set afterwards from
Add-Ins > Scripting Tools > Preferences (addinUserPrefMenu.jsl).

Section: Globals
*/

Names default to here( 1 );

thisAddIn = "com.github.himanga.JMPScriptingTools";

If(
	!Namespace Exists( Eval( thisAddIn ) || ".addinnamespace" ),
	ns = New Namespace( Eval( thisAddIn ) || ".addinnamespace" ),
	ns = Namespace( Eval( thisAddIn ) || ".addinnamespace" )
);

/*
	Function: ShowLoggingFirstRunWindow
		---Prototype---
		ShowLoggingFirstRunWindow()
		---------------
		Show the local-logging disclosure with an on/off choice. Clicking
		OK saves the answer to the "LogLevel" preference, which is what
		marks the notice as answered. Cancel or the window X saves
		nothing, so the notice returns on the next load.

	Returns:
		The level the user chose, or "" if they cancelled.

	Example:
		> ns:ShowLoggingFirstRunWindow();
*/
ns:ShowLoggingFirstRunWindow = Function( {}, {chosen, introText, result, rb},

	chosen = "";

	introText = ns:metadata_aa["name"] || " can keep a local diagnostic log on " ||
		"this machine to help troubleshoot problems - it is never uploaded or " ||
		"sent anywhere. The log includes your Windows username and computer " ||
		"name (for telling sessions apart when troubleshooting), plus which " ||
		"commands you ran and any errors.\!N\!N" ||
		"Nothing is logged until you choose below. You can change this any " ||
		"time from Add-Ins > Scripting Tools > Preferences, where you can also " ||
		"pick a more detailed level (Warn or Debug) for troubleshooting.";

	// A modal New Window returns a result associative array (["button"] is 1
	// for OK, -1 for Cancel) - NOT a window reference, and not until it has
	// closed. So there is nothing to send Close Window to from inside a
	// button script; JMP closes a modal itself when OK or Cancel is clicked.
	// The choice is captured in OK's script, which runs before the close.
	result = New Window( "Scripting Tools Logging",
		<< Modal,
		V List Box(
			Text Box( "Logging", << Set Font Size( 20 ), << Set Width( 480 ) ),
			Spacer Box( Size( 0, 10 ) ),
			Text Box( introText, << Set Width( 480 ), << Set Wrap( 480 ) ),
			Spacer Box( Size( 0, 20 ) ),

			rb = Radio Box( {"Keep a local log (recommended)", "Do not log anything"} ),
			Spacer Box( Size( 0, 20 ) ),

			Text Box( "Log file location:", << Set Font Style( "bold" ), << Set Width( 480 ) ),
			Text Edit Box( ns:LogFilePath,
				<< Set Read Only( 1 ), << Set Width( 480 ), << Set NLines( 2 ), << Set Wrap( 480 )
			),
			Spacer Box( Size( 0, 20 ) ),

			H List Box(
				Button Box( "OK",
					chosen = If( (rb << Get) == 1, "Info", "Off" );
				),
				Button Box( "Cancel" ),
				<< Padding( Left( 0 ), Top( 0 ), Right( 20 ), Bottom( 0 ) )
			),
			<< Padding( Left( 20 ), Top( 20 ), Right( 20 ), Bottom( 20 ) )
		)
	);

	// Cancel or the window X leaves the preference unset, so nothing is
	// logged and the notice appears again next load - closing without
	// choosing is deliberately not consent.
	If( result["button"] == 1 & chosen != "",
		ns:UpdatePreference( "LogLevel", chosen );
	);

	chosen;
);
